<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shenzhen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shenzhen is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangdong">Guangdong</a> province in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a>. In 1980 it became one of China's first Special Economic Zones under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deng-xiaoping">Deng Xiaoping</a>'s reforms, and it grew from a small market town into a metropolis of more than 17 million people, a centre of manufacturing, electronics and technology companies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shenzhen.jpg" alt="Shenzhen" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charlie fong · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Commercial_area_of_futian_to_east2020.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
